 pub-id-type="pmid">1763061</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The route of enteric infection in notmal mice</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1974</year><volume>139</volume><fpage>1189</fpage><lpage>1203</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4596512</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="other">Arias, I.M., J.L. Boyer, N. Fausto, W.B. Jakoby, D.A.  Schachter, and D.A. Shafritz. 1994. The Liver: Biology and  Pathobiology. Raven Press Ltd., New York. 1628 pp.</citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wessendorf</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Brelje</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Which fluorophore is brightest? A comparison of staining obtained using Fluorescein, Tetramethylrhodamine Lissamine Rhodamine, Texas Red, and Cyanine 3.18</article-title><source>Histochemistry</source><year>1992</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1429023</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="other">Rubin, R.H., and L. Weinstein. 1977. Salmonellosis: microbiologic, pathologic and clinical features. Stratton Intercontinental Medical Book Corp., New York. 137 pp.</citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Faulstich</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Zobeley</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rinnerthaler</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Small</surname><given-names>JV<